.env
.venv/
__pycache__/
*.pyc
.pytest_cache/
.coverage
.coverage.*
htmlcov/
data/
.DS_Store
*.egg-info/
build/
dist/
.mypy_cache/
.ruff_cache/
.claude/worktrees/
backups/
tests/eval/baselines/*.json
logs/

# Stray SQLite-style artifact created at the repo root by accidental tooling
# (the project's database is Postgres — there is no app-owned brain.db). Ignored
# so it can never be committed by mistake. Anchored to the root only.
/brain.db

# Runtime shim cache for the brain CLI launcher (T1.5).
# `_launcher.ensure_shim()` copies package-data bash templates here on
# first invocation. Dev-checkouts get `<repo>/.shims/`; pipx users get
# `~/.brain/.shims/`. Never tracked.
.shims/

# Runtime pid dir for the brain daemons (watch + build watchers). The fg
# wrappers write `$BRAIN_HOME/run/brain-{watch,build}.pid` here; in a
# dev-checkout $BRAIN_HOME is the repo root, so `run/` lands in the tree.
# Moved off /tmp because macOS's tmp_cleaner reaped the long-lived pid files.
# Never tracked.
run/

# Playwright MCP server scratch dir (browser-automation traces/screenshots/session
# state from MCP browser tool runs). Transient local artifact — never tracked.
.playwright-mcp/

# Brainstorm artifacts (kept local-only — can contain PII / personal references)
.superpowers/

# Plans / audits / QA — local-only working docs (may contain personal
# references). docs/ is private-by-subdir: the publishable reference docs
# (docs/README.md, docs/cli-reference.md, docs/graphrag.md,
# docs/vault-and-wiki.md, docs/configuration.md), docs/guides/, docs/assets/,
# docs/specs/, and docs/plans/ stay trackable; everything below is ignored. Add
# any NEW private subdir/file to this list before it can leak.
#
# docs/specs/ was un-ignored deliberately: CLAUDE.md rule 11b mandates that all
# specs live there, so leaving it ignored meant every design doc in the project
# was one clean checkout from being lost. It was PII-scrubbed first and is now
# synthetic-only, exactly like tests and fixtures — keep it that way (rule 15).
#
# docs/plans/ was un-ignored on the same grounds and the same terms: rule 11b
# mandates that plans live there too, so an ignored plan is one clean checkout
# from gone. Scanned before landing — no PII values, no real corpus identifiers.
#
# docs/audits/ STAYS IGNORED. This is a decision, not an oversight: do NOT
# "finish the job" by moving it up beside docs/plans/. Its files are clean of
# PII *values*, so the usual test passes — and that test is the wrong one here.
# This repository is PUBLIC, and its history still carries real personal data
# that has never been rewritten (removing it would mean rewriting ~446 commits,
# which is destructive and has not been authorised). docs/audits/ holds the PII
# audit, which is a precise index INTO that history: hundreds of findings across
# dozens of files in dozens of named commit SHAs, each labelled by category.
# Committing it would turn an expensive scan into a single `git show`. A file
# that contains no PII can still be a map to PII. The map should keep existing —
# just not inside the repository it maps.
docs/audits/
docs/notes/
docs/qa/
docs/summaries/
docs/launch/
docs/elicit-slack-blurb.txt
docs/HOW-TO-TEST-elicit.md

# Real GraphRAG alias rules contain real entity names (CLAUDE.md rule 15) — keep local.
# The checked-in file is aliases/default.yml.example (synthetic, documentation only).
/graph_aliases.yml
/src/brain/graph_rag/aliases/default.yml

# Real PII-gate denylist (real names/customers/codenames) — keep local (rule 15).
# The checked-in file is .pii-denylist.local.txt.example (synthetic).
/.pii-denylist.local.txt

# Generated audio-overview artifacts (brain audio) — real content, never commit
audio/

# Ad-hoc screenshots dropped at the repo root during UI/design work (e.g.
# `w5-1440-light.png` from the wave-5 web-UI pass). Root-level only, so
# committed assets under docs/ or src/ are unaffected. Kept out of history
# because they are one-off working artifacts, not deliverables — and because a
# stray root PNG is exactly what a `git add -A` sweeps into a release commit.
/*.png
/*.jpg
/*.jpeg
